  "assumptions": [
    "Only scalar continuous/categorical cell values are sampled. Categorical values require nearest; vector components are not rotated and field units/values are not converted.",
    "Explicit target geometry defines cell centres. Bilinear uses the existing strict nodata sampler: every contributing cell must be valid; edge cells cover the outer half-cell. No gap filling or extrapolation beyond the source footprint.",
    "Only XY coordinates are transformed. No height/datum reduction, measurement continuation, temporal epoch correction, antialiasing, area-conservative averaging or uncertainty propagation occurs.",
    "Cross-CRS support is limited to the documented shared 2D EPSG set. Python uses pyproj/PROJ with XY order and no ballpark operations; JavaScript uses the existing proj4 definitions with approximate Australian datum transformations. Datum policy backend is an explicit acknowledgement, not a survey-grade accuracy claim.",
    "Unknown/custom CRS labels may be resampled without a CRS change when equal and coordinate units are declared. Unreferenced local grids require explicit matching frame IDs and units.",
    "Coordinate/transport/support/uncertainty metadata that no longer describes the output is retained in flat input lineage rather than copied as active target metadata. Other scientific metadata/correction declarations are preserved.",
    "Source values and metadata are preserved. Returned masks describe coordinate validity, footprint and per-band sampling support, not calibrated geological uncertainty. Direct APIs leave raster workflow v1 unchanged."
  ],
  "references": [
    "https://pyproj4.github.io/pyproj/stable/api/transformer.html",
    "https://proj4js.org/"
  ]
